-- 1 Computing basics
(1,'What does CPU stand for?','Central Processing Unit','Central Program Utility','Computer Personal Unit','Core Processing Utility',0,'It is often called the brain of the computer.'),
(1,'Which of these is volatile memory?','Hard disk','RAM','SSD','DVD',1,'It loses its contents when the power goes off.'),
(1,'The binary number system uses which base?','8','10','2','16',2,'Only two digits are used: 0 and 1.'),
(1,'Which of these is an operating system?','Chrome','Python','Excel','Linux',3,'Windows and macOS belong to the same group.'),
(1,'How many bits are in one byte?','8','4','16','10',0,'Think of a standard character such as the letter A.'),
(1,'Which of these is an input device?','Monitor','Printer','Keyboard','Speaker',2,'You use it to send data into the computer.'),
(1,'Which of these is a programming language?','Windows','Python','Ethernet','USB',1,'It is named after a comedy group, not a snake.'),
(1,'Which storage unit is the largest?','Byte','Kilobyte','Gigabyte','Megabyte',2,'Each step up is roughly a thousand times bigger.'),
-- 2 Web development
(2,'Which HTML tag creates a hyperlink?','<link>','<a>','<href>','<url>',1,'It is the anchor tag.'),
(2,'Which CSS property changes the colour of text?','color','font-color','text-style','foreground',0,'It uses the American spelling.'),
(2,'Which HTTP status code means Not Found?','200','301','404','500',2,'The most famous error on the web.'),
(2,'Which method selects an element by its id in JavaScript?','getElementsByClass','document.find','document.select','document.getElementById',3,'The name says exactly what it does.'),
(2,'In PHP, which superglobal holds data sent from a form using method POST?','$_POST','$_FORM','$_GET','$_DATA',0,'It is named after the HTTP method.'),
(2,'What does the SQL SELECT statement do?','Deletes rows','Reads rows from a table','Creates a table','Changes a password',1,'It is used for reading, not changing, data.'),
(2,'What does CSS stand for?','Cascading Style Sheets','Creative Style System','Computer Style Syntax','Colour and Style Sheets',0,'It controls how HTML looks.'),
(2,'Which HTML element is used for the biggest heading?','<head>','<title>','<header>','<h1>',3,'Headings run from 1 to 6.'),
-- 3 Programming logic
(3,'Which keyword starts a condition in JavaScript?','for','while','if','loop',2,'If this is true, then do that.'),
(3,'What is the index of the first item in a JavaScript array?','0','1','-1','2',0,'Most programming languages count from zero.'),
(3,'What is a function?','A kind of variable','A reusable block of code','A loop counter','A comment',1,'You write it once and call it many times.'),
(3,'What does 7 % 3 give?','0','2','3','1',3,'The % operator returns the remainder.'),
(3,'Which loop repeats while a condition stays true?','while','if','switch','return',0,'The name is also an English word for "during".'),
(3,'What does typeof "hello" return in JavaScript?','text','string','char','word',1,'It is the name of the data type.'),
(3,'What does === check in JavaScript?','Only the value','Assigns a value','Equal value and equal type','Greater than',2,'It is stricter than ==.'),
(3,'Which array method adds an item to the end?','push','pop','shift','slice',0,'Its opposite is pop.'),
-- 4 Data structures and algorithms
(4,'Which order does a stack follow?','FIFO','Random','LIFO','Sorted',2,'Think of a pile of plates.'),
(4,'Which order does a queue follow?','FIFO','LIFO','Random','Reverse',0,'First come, first served.'),
(4,'Binary search only works when the data is...','Random','Sorted','Unique','Negative',1,'You need to know which half to throw away.'),
(4,'What is the time complexity of binary search?','O(n)','O(1)','O(n^2)','O(log n)',3,'The search space halves every step.'),
(4,'What does a brute force approach do?','Tries every possibility','Guesses once','Sorts first','Uses recursion only',0,'Simple, but can be very slow.'),
(4,'What is the worst case of linear search?','O(1)','O(log n)','O(n)','O(n^2)',2,'You may have to check every item.'),
(4,'Which of these is a sorting algorithm?','Hash map','Bubble sort','Linked list','Stack',1,'Small values bubble up to the top.'),
(4,'A linked list node holds data and a...','Index number','Hash key','Array size','Pointer to the next node',3,'This is how nodes connect to each other.'),
